% minor_loss — the pressure lost at a bend, valve, tee, sudden change or entrance
%
% Usage:      dp = minor_loss(K, rho, v)
% Computes:   dp = K rho v^2 / 2, with K the loss coefficient of the fitting (from a table for that fitting).
% Method:     the definition of the loss coefficient.
% Units:      SI: rho kg/m3, v m/s, dp Pa. K has no unit.
% References: Incropera et al., Fundamentals of Heat and Mass Transfer, 7th ed., eq. 8.52 (the loss form); K values: the
%             fitting's own table (this function holds none: a hidden constant would have no source).
% Check:      K 0.9 (a 90 degree bend), rho 1000, v 3 m/s: dp = 4050 Pa (tools/field-test/eng.mjs).
function dp = minor_loss(K, rho, v)
dp = K * rho * v ^ 2 / 2;
end
